And from the fact that Medusa had two sisters as ugly as herself whom 
she saw on a day-by-day basis - without turning into stone, evidently, - 
you may note another difference between nethack and the lore.  The 
Medusa of the ancient Greeks would turn *others* to stone by looking at 
them but not herself...  She might not be attracted by her mirror image, 
but it would not kill her.  By the way, Perseus used her reflection in 
his shield to see her, so I take it that her reflected image should not 
kill anyone.  Only if you looked at her directly, would she stone you, 
so it is even less likely that she gets killed by looking into a mirror.

